|~ `::construct`, the step that puts a value under a tag through the
   tag's constructor, `::T[…]`, and what is declared under it: its
   constructor and the refusals of that step.
   The decisions it exists for: [D114]. ~|

:construct
  |~~ The step that puts a payload under a tag, `::T[…]`, `::T{…}`,
      `::T(…)` or `::T"…"`, through the tag's constructor, which checks
      or builds the value.

      In a quote the step is a record, `~(::Box[1 2]) | first` answering
      `::construct{:tag ::Box :payload [1 2]}`: `:tag` the tag and
      `:payload` the step of its payload.
      ::link~(::tagged | doc) ::link~(::qlang/pipeline | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps
        |~~ The record of a constructor invocation, `:tag` and `:payload`,
            built into its step, which reads back as itself.
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotSchemaError
        |~~ A `::construct` is a map of `:tag`, a tag name, and
            `:payload`, a step, both given, and `:field` names the field
            that does not fit: the tag is written with its two colons, so
            the step `::Box[1]` is
            `{:tag ::Box :payload [1]} | tag ::construct`.
            ::link~(::construct | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :ReadBackDiffersError
        |~~ The `::construct` prints as text that reads back as another
            step, and `:printed` is that text: a payload that opens with a
            name, a digit or a slash joins its tag, `::Box42` a name of
            its own. Such a payload is written as a group, the step
            `::Box(42)`, whose record holds the group,
            `{:tag ::Box :payload (~((42)) | first)}`.
            ::link~(::construct | doc)
        ~~|
    | throws :TagNotKindError
        |~~ The tag before a payload addresses a kind, a label declared by
            its chain or by its page alone, a word, whose args it lays
            itself over, `::vec/take[2]`, or no declaration at all; a tag
            that addresses a name holding a value of its own names nothing
            to build by, and `:tag` is that tag. The value is read by its
            name, `limit`, and is put under a tag of its own,
            `::Limit(limit)`.
            ::link~(::construct | doc)
        ~~|
    | carries :TagNotKindError/tag
        |~~ The tag, whose node is neither a label nor a word. ~~|
        ::tag
    | proves :holdsTheTagAndThePayload
        |~~ The step holds its tag and its payload. ~~|
        ~(~(::Box[1 2]) | first | get [/tag /payload] | eq [::Box [1 2]])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesATagThatIsAKeyword
        |~~ A `:tag` that is a keyword is refused, `:field` naming it. ~~|
        ~(::construct{:tag :Box :payload [1]}
          !| [type (get /field)] | eq [::construct/PayloadNotSchemaError :tag])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesARecordWithoutAPayload
        |~~ A record without its payload is refused, `:field` naming it. ~~|
        ~({:tag ::Box} | tag ::construct
          !| [type (get /field)] | eq [::construct/PayloadNotSchemaError :payload])
    | proves :PayloadNotSchemaError/buildsTheStepOfATag
        |~~ A tag name and the step of a payload build the step. ~~|
        ~({:tag ::Box :payload [1]} | tag ::construct | get [it] | tag ::quote | eq ~(::Box[1]))
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAPayloadThatJoinsItsTag
        |~~ A number payload prints joined to its tag, which reads back as
            another name.
        ~~|
        ~(::construct{:tag ::Box :payload 42}
          !| [type (get /printed)] | eq [::construct/ReadBackDiffersError "::Box42"])
    | proves :ReadBackDiffersError/writesThePayloadAsAGroup
        |~~ A payload in a group reads back as itself. ~~|
        ~({:tag ::Box :payload (~((42)) | first)} | tag ::construct
          | get [it] | tag ::quote | eq ~(::Box(42)))
    | proves :TagNotKindError/refusesTheTagOfAValue
        |~~ The tag of a name that holds a value builds nothing. ~~|
        ~(:limit 5 | ::limit[1]
          !| [type (get /tag) (get /actualType)] | eq [::construct/TagNotKindError ::limit ::number])
    | proves :TagNotKindError/laysAWordsTagOverItsArgs
        |~~ The tag of a word lays itself over its args. ~~|
        ~(::vec/take[2] | type | eq ::vec/take)
    | proves :TagNotKindError/putsTheValueUnderATagOfItsOwn
        |~~ The value of a name is put under a tag of its own. ~~|
        ~(:limit 5 | ::Limit(limit) | payload | eq 5)
    | impl ::builtin{}

